      "node": "settler_colonialism",
      "field": "focus",
      "old": "Co-citation places Daschuk's Plains history next to Wolfe and Veracini (19 of 58 Wolfe/Veracini-citing PhDs). Its own framing is unchecked, so this is a comparison strand.",
      "new": "Daschuk's Plains history is the work most co-cited with Wolfe and Veracini by Canadian PhDs (19 of 58, lift 10.2; a 2020–25 entrant with support 12; History PhD citation graph, release 2026-10-23). Its publisher describes 'a policy of starvation' that 'sparked widespread debate about genocide in Canada' and does not use 'settler colonialism'; the 2019 edition adds responses by Kelm, Mosby, Neylan and Woolford. His own framing remains unchecked; the TRC summary's 'cultural genocide' (2015) is the public text beside which the book is read. A comparison strand.",
      "reason": "Period-4 wave 1, 2026-10-23 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-settler-colonial.md) P.2: publisher page read; framing still unchecked.",
