      "new": "Comparative settler economies (1983) and gender, race, ethnicity and class in settler societies (1995) are earlier comparative scholarship, before the field's theoretical consolidation; Veracini's history of the concept records decolonization-era usage of the term itself. Veracini (2013) reads the 'settler/dominion capitalism' literature as writing 'indigenous people and indigenous history off the conceptual map'; Kauanui (2016, n. 7) adds Sayegh 1965, Rodinson 1973, Sayigh 1979 and Trask 1992/2000 before Wolfe.",
