    {
      "id": "derrida_archive_primary",
      "field": "verification.note",
      "expect": "Title, copyright and lecture note, complete printed pp. 1–5 including p. 4 note 1, and pp. 7–15 read. Distinguishes archive/authority/consignation from spontaneous memory, explicitly uses Combe, and reworks Freud’s destruction drive and Mystic Pad with questions about recording technologies. Theoretical claims are attributed, not empirical confirmation. Freud, Combe and the earlier Derrida essay quoted here are not independently collated. Later argument, including the developed Yerushalmi exchange, remains unread. French/Diacritics 1995, English book 1996 and paperback dates are not conflated.",
      "value": "Title, copyright and lecture note, complete printed pp. 1–5 including p. 4 note 1, and pp. 7–15 read. Distinguishes archive/authority/consignation from spontaneous memory, explicitly uses Combe, and reworks Freud’s destruction drive and Mystic Pad with questions about recording technologies. Theoretical claims are attributed, not empirical confirmation. Freud, Combe and the earlier Derrida essay quoted here are not independently collated. Later argument, including the developed Yerushalmi exchange, remains unread. French/Diacritics 1995, English book 1996 and paperback dates are not conflated. Period-4 wave 1 (2026-10-23): the reading of 2026-09-12 was made through a PDF on a mirror host of the kind the 2026-10-19 provenance rule excludes; the link is replaced by the University of Chicago Press page (fetched 2026-10-23: © 1996, viii + 114 pp., Religion and Postmodernism), which does not reproduce the text, and the Diacritics printing is recorded as p4a_derrida_diacritics_1995 (DOI 10.2307/465144). The passages have not been re-read through an eligible route; edge_587–589 and the roster rows stand on the earlier record."
