{"id":"p4a_hartman_venus_2008","title":"Saidiya Hartman, \"Venus in Two Acts,\" Small Axe 12:2 (no. 26), June 2008: 1–14.","citation":"Saidiya Hartman, \"Venus in Two Acts,\" Small Axe 12:2 (no. 26), June 2008: 1–14.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1215/-12-2-1","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref only (1 June 2008, pp. 1–14); Duke's journal platform returned 403 and Project MUSE a challenge page; unread. Copies on course sites were not opened."}}
{"id":"p4a_hartman_macarthur_2019","title":"MacArthur Foundation, \"Saidiya Hartman,\" MacArthur Fellows, class of 2019 (published 25 September 2019).","citation":"MacArthur Foundation, \"Saidiya Hartman,\" MacArthur Fellows, class of 2019 (published 25 September 2019).","url":"https://www.macfound.org/fellows/class-of-2019/saidiya-hartman","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Read in full: BA Wesleyan 1984, PhD Yale 1992, Berkeley 1992–2006, Columbia; \"a speculative method she terms 'critical fabulation,' which questions historical archives as the sole source of credible information about the past\"; books 1997, 2007, 2019."}}
{"id":"p4a_fuentes_dispossessed_2016","title":"Marisa J. Fuentes, Dispossessed Lives: Enslaved Women, Violence, and the Archive (Philadelphia: University of Pennsylvania Press, 2016).","citation":"Marisa J. Fuentes, Dispossessed Lives: Enslaved Women, Violence, and the Archive (Philadelphia: University of Pennsylvania Press, 2016).","url":"https://www.pennpress.org/9780812224184/dispossessed-lives/","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Penn Press page returned 403; description read on the Google Books (CA) record (2016, 217 pp.): \"Fuentes interrogates the archive and its historical production\"; body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_farge_allure_2013","title":"Arlette Farge, The Allure of the Archives, trans. Thomas Scott-Railton, foreword by Natalie Zemon Davis (New Haven: Yale University Press, 2013; paperback 2015); original Le Goût de l'archive (Paris: Seuil, 1989).","citation":"Arlette Farge, The Allure of the Archives, trans. Thomas Scott-Railton, foreword by Natalie Zemon Davis (New Haven: Yale University Press, 2013; paperback 2015); original Le Goût de l'archive (Paris: Seuil, 1989).","url":"https://yalebooks.yale.edu/book/9780300198935/the-allure-of-the-archives/","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Yale page read (e-book 24 September 2013; paperback 24 February 2015, 152 pp.; \"the original was published in 1989\"; blurbs by Hunt, Soll, Wineapple, Price, Burns; 2014 translation prize). Seuil page 404; body unread."}}
