{"id":"ann_laura_stoler","label":"Ann Laura Stoler","date_label":"'Tensions of Empire' (with Cooper) 1989 · Race and the Education of Desire 1995 · Tensions of Empire 1997 · 'Tense and Tender Ties' 2001 · 'Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance' 2002 · Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power 2002 · Haunted by Empire 2006 · Along the Archival Grain 2009 · Imperial Debris 2013 · Duress 2016","layer":"historians","period":null,"hunt_core_paradigm":false,"description":"An American anthropologist of Dutch and French colonial rule whose work moved from the plantation belt of Sumatra to the colonial archive itself. With Frederick Cooper she set an agenda for reading metropole and colony together (1989; Tensions of Empire, 1997). Race and the Education of Desire (1995) asked why 'Foucault's elusive and suggestive treatment of race still remains so marginal to what colonial historians take from him' (2002, p. 141, as quoted by Ottevaere); Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power (2002) treated 'colonizer/colonized' not 'as a given' but as 'a historically shifting pair of social categories that needs to be explained' (p. 13). 'Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance' (2002) asked scholars to move 'from archive-as-source to archive-as-subject'; Along the Archival Grain (2009) read Dutch records 'along the grain' for 'the pulse of the archive' and 'the habits of a colonial heart'. Dutch reviewers found the pulses hard to identify and Indonesian archives absent. Imperial Debris (2013) and Duress (2016) turned to ruination and 'imperial durabilities'. Gouda: in postcolonial studies 'paying homage to Ann Stoler's work has become de rigueur' (2009).","representative_figures_and_works":"Ann Laura Stoler (b. 1949); Capitalism and Confrontation in Sumatra's Plantation Belt, 1870–1979 (1985); with Frederick Cooper, 'Tensions of Empire' (American Ethnologist, 1989) and Tensions of Empire (eds, 1997); Race and the Education of Desire (1995); 'Tense and Tender Ties' (JAH, 2001); 'Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance' (Archival Science, 2002); Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power (2002; 2nd ed. 2010); ed., Haunted by Empire (2006); with McGranahan and Perdue, eds, Imperial Formations (2007); Along the Archival Grain (2009); ed., Imperial Debris (2013); Duress (2016); Interior Frontiers (2022). Readers: Dawn Ottevaere (2004); Frances Gouda, Remco Raben, Henk Schulte Nordholt (2009); Ronald Schultz (2015).","entry_kind":"person","entry_type":"Individual thinker or historian","scope_note":"Read on 2026-10-23 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §§1–2, 6): the abstract and reference list of the 2002 Archival Science essay; the contents of Along the Archival Grain and three reviews from the Bijdragen debate (Gouda and Schulte Nordholt in full, Raben's first page) with the first paragraph of Stoler's reply; Ottevaere's H-Net review of Carnal Knowledge (in full) and the UC Press contents; Schultz's H-Net review of Imperial Debris (in full); the Duke pages for Haunted by Empire and Duress. Unread: every book's body, the 2002 essay's body, 'Tense and Tender Ties' (2001), the Cooper–Stoler introductions of 1989 and 1997 (metadata and contents only, as the graph already records), Imperial Formations (2007), Interior Frontiers (2022), and Stoler's reply to her Dutch critics beyond its opening. Her 2002 notes cite Trouillot's Silencing the Past three times; no sentence of hers on Trouillot was read. Quotations from the 2009 book are 'as quoted by' Gouda or Schulte Nordholt, from Carnal Knowledge 'as quoted by' Ottevaere, from Imperial Debris 'as quoted by' Schultz, with their page numbers. Wikidata Q16203101 checked by QLever on 2026-10-23 (born 1949; anthropologist, historian; VIAF 263247736). Posts from the New School's pages (search rendering; the page itself returned 429) and the UC Press author line; the Wisconsin years (1983–89) and degrees (Barnard BA 1972, Columbia PhD 1982) from Wikipedia's citation of New School pages, orientation only; the 1985 book is not dated as an event because no publisher page was fetched. History PhD citation graph (release 2026-10-23): cited by 10.7% of Canada + US theses in 2020–25, the strongest riser of 2015–25, in 11 of 18 fields; Along the Archival Grain 4.4% and Carnal Knowledge 3.8% of theses 2015–25 (figures for this note, not for arrows).","source_ids":["cooper_stoler_tensions_1997","digital10_source_digital07_hegarty_platformization","p4a_burton_archive_stories_2005","p4a_cooper_stoler_ae_1989","p4a_from_the_margins_2002","p4a_gouda_bki_2009","p4a_ottevaere_hnet_2004","p4a_raben_bki_2009","p4a_schulte_nordholt_bki_2009","p4a_schultz_hnet_2015","p4a_stoler_archival_grain_2009","p4a_stoler_archives_2002","p4a_stoler_bki_reply_2009","p4a_stoler_carnal_2002","p4a_stoler_debris_2013","p4a_stoler_duress_2016","p4a_stoler_haunted_2006","p4a_stoler_newschool_profile","p4a_stoler_refiguring_2002","p4a_stoler_tense_2001","pe139_perry_presence_2001","pe139_perry_sick_1995","stoler_desire"],"coverage":{"reviewed_through":2016,"basis":"Works dated through Duress (2016) from publisher pages and reviews read on 2026-10-23; later work (Interior Frontiers, 2022; the 2019 French edition of the archive book) is named in the scope note only; the 2024 web-archives essay is a reception event."},"chronology":{"version":1,"label":"Selected contributions · 1989–2016; reception 2004–24","selection_note":"Selected dated contributions and readings; not career or lifespan boundaries.","events":[{"id":"als_cooper_ae_1989","label":"With Cooper, 'Introduction. Tensions of Empire: Colonial Control and Visions of Rule', American Ethnologist 16:4","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":1989,"month":11,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_cooper_stoler_ae_1989"],"support":"Crossref (vol. 16, no. 4, pp. 609–621, November 1989); unread."},{"id":"als_desire_1995","label":"Race and the Education of Desire: Foucault's History of Sexuality and the Colonial Order of Things (Duke)","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":1995,"month":10,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:stoler_desire"],"support":"Existing graph source (Duke page, October 1995; body unread)."},{"id":"als_tensions_1997","label":"With Cooper, eds, Tensions of Empire: Colonial Cultures in a Bourgeois World (UC Press), opening chapter 'Between Metropole and Colony'","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":1997,"month":2,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:cooper_stoler_tensions_1997"],"support":"Existing graph source (contents; February 1997); chapter unread."},{"id":"als_tense_2001","label":"'Tense and Tender Ties: The Politics of Comparison in North American History and (Post) Colonial Studies', JAH 88:3","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2001,"month":12,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_tense_2001"],"support":"Crossref (December 2001, from p. 829); unread."},{"id":"als_archives_2002","label":"'Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance', Archival Science 2:1–2, 87–109; reprinted in Refiguring the Archive","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2002,"month":3,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_archives_2002","graph:p4a_stoler_refiguring_2002"],"support":"Crossref (March 2002); abstract and notes read."},{"id":"als_carnal_2002","label":"Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power: Race and the Intimate in Colonial Rule (UC Press; 2nd ed. with a new preface, 2010)","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2002,"precision":"year"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_carnal_2002","graph:p4a_ottevaere_hnet_2004"],"support":"UC Press page (2010 edition); Ottevaere gives the 2002 edition."},{"id":"als_negatives_2002","label":"'Developing Historical Negatives: Race and the (Modernist) Visions of a Colonial State', in From the Margins (Duke)","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2002,"month":6,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_from_the_margins_2002"],"support":"Duke contents (p. 156); later ch. 4 of Along the Archival Grain (MUSE contents)."},{"id":"als_ottevaere_2004","label":"Ottevaere's review of Carnal Knowledge, H-Women","kind":"reception_publication","track":"reception","date":{"year":2004,"month":6,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_ottevaere_hnet_2004"],"support":"Read in full."},{"id":"als_newschool_2004","label":"Joins The New School for Social Research; founding chair of the revitalised Anthropology Department","kind":"office","track":"context","date":{"year":2004,"precision":"year"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_newschool_profile"],"support":"New School page as rendered by a search engine only (the page returned 429); source marked not_checked. Drop if a read page is required."},{"id":"als_haunted_2006","label":"Ed., Haunted by Empire: Geographies of Intimacy in North American History (Duke), with 'Intimidations of Empire' and 'Tense and Tender Ties'","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2006,"month":5,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_haunted_2006"],"support":"Duke page (contents)."},{"id":"als_grain_2009","label":"Along the Archival Grain: Epistemic Anxieties and Colonial Common Sense (Princeton; © 2008)","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2009,"precision":"year"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_archival_grain_2009","graph:p4a_gouda_bki_2009"],"support":"MUSE record; Gouda's citation."},{"id":"als_bki_2009","label":"Bijdragen 165:4 debate: Gouda, Raben, Schulte Nordholt; Stoler's reply 'Thinking through colonial ontologies'","kind":"reception_publication","track":"reception","date":{"year":2009,"precision":"year"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_gouda_bki_2009","graph:p4a_raben_bki_2009","graph:p4a_schulte_nordholt_bki_2009","graph:p4a_stoler_bki_reply_2009"],"support":"Two reviews read in full; the reply's first paragraph."},{"id":"als_debris_2013","label":"Ed., Imperial Debris: On Ruins and Ruination (Duke), with 'The Rot Remains: From Ruins to Ruination'","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2013,"precision":"year"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_debris_2013","graph:p4a_schultz_hnet_2015"],"support":"Schultz's review gives \"Duke University Press, 2013. 384 pp.\" and both ISBNs."},{"id":"als_schultz_2015","label":"Schultz's review of Imperial Debris, H-Empire","kind":"reception_publication","track":"reception","date":{"year":2015,"month":2,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_schultz_hnet_2015"],"support":"Read in full."},{"id":"als_duress_2016","label":"Duress: Imperial Durabilities in Our Times (Duke)","kind":"publication","track":"contributions","date":{"year":2016,"month":11,"precision":"month"},"source_ids":["graph:p4a_stoler_duress_2016"],"support":"Duke page (November 2016, 448 pp., contents)."},{"id":"als_hegarty_2024","label":"'Web archives after platformization: reading social media collections along the archival grain' (Hegarty), on the web_history entry","kind":"reception_publication","track":"reception","date":{"year":2024,"precision":"year"},"source_ids":["graph:digital10_source_digital07_hegarty_platformization"],"support":"Existing graph source; the title borrows her phrase; not re-read this wave."}],"intervals":[],"continuation":{"status":"not_asserted","basis":"No continuous duration or ending is established by this selection."},"interpretation":"Selected dated contributions and readings. The 2009 Bijdragen debate is dated by its parts, not as an interval; the group entry archival_turn holds the field's chronology. Unread books are dated from publisher records; the 2004 appointment rests on a page not read directly.","prepared_on":"2026-10-23","editorial_record":"data/production-batches/group-revision-1.156/acceptance.json"}}
