proposed_edges [{"proposal_id":"p4B_rel_07","source":"settler_colonialism","target":"patrick_wolfe","type":"critique","relationship_kind":"critique","directed":true,"relationship":"The field's critics answer Wolfe by name: a structure that 'posits a structural inevitability' and risks 'colonial fatalism' (Macoun and Strakosch 2013); a 'teleology of elimination' (Rowse 2014); a slogan that 'stand[s]-in for a serious engagement of his theory' and a field that 'cannot replace Indigenous Studies' (Kauanui 2016); elimination against exploitation (Englert 2020)","map_label":"Critiques of the Wolfe-an model, 2013–20","evidence_note":"Macoun and Strakosch 2013 (author version, read): \"SCT can depict colonization as structurally inevitable\"; \"Foundational scholar Patrick Wolfe has been labelled 'very much a structuralist stuck in a poststructuralist world'\"; \"a kind of colonial fatalism\"; \"it does not account for Indigenous lives\". Snelgrove, Dhamoon and Corntassel 2014 (read): \"treating settler colonialism as a meta-structure, thus erasing both its contingency and the dynamics that co-constitute\" it. Rowse 2014 (abstract, existing): a \"teleology of elimination\". Kauanui 2016 (read in full): a critique that defends the theory and asks that \"Settler Colonial Studies does not, should not, and cannot replace Indigenous Studies\". Englert 2020 (read in full): \"a critique of the Wolfe-an model\"; elimination \"does not accurately define the overall logic of settler colonialism, as claimed by Wolfe\". Fairness: Kauanui and Goeman record his disclaimers and his engagement with NAIS; Macoun and Strakosch call his contribution \"vital\". (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-settler-colonial.md)","source_ids":["p4b_macoun_strakosch_2013_qut","screq_snelgrove_dhamoon_corntassel_2014","screq_rowse_2014","screq_kauanui_2016","p4b_englert_2020"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review"},{"proposal_id":"p4B_rel_14","source":"settler_colonialism","target":"dependency","type":"connection","relationship_kind":"comparison","directed":false,"relationship":"Settler colonialism against underdevelopment: the 1970s–80s 'settler/dominion capitalism' literature made the settler colony 'the opposite of colonialism and associated underdevelopment' (Veracini 2013 on Denoon 1983); Englert returns the question through Harvey's accumulation by dispossession (2020)","map_label":"Settler capitalism and dependency","evidence_note":"Veracini 2013 (abstract, existing record; author manuscript read): in the third phase \"settler colonialism is understood as the opposite of colonialism and associated underdevelopment and political fragmentation\", and the settler-capitalism approach wrote \"indigenous people and indigenous history off the conceptual map\". Denoon 1983 at title level (existing). Englert 2020 (read in full): accumulation by dispossession \"as developed by David Harvey (2003)\" proposed as the alternative to the elimination model, with Emmanuel's 1972 NLR essay on white-settler colonialism in his bibliography. A comparison of frames; no descent asserted. (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-settler-colonial.md)","source_ids":["p4b_veracini_2013_deposit","screq_veracini_2013","screq_denoon_1983","p4b_englert_2020"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review"},{"proposal_id":"p4B_rel_15","source":"settler_colonialism","target":"cdn_working_class","type":"connection","relationship_kind":"contribution","directed":true,"relationship":"The settler order as a frame for Canadian working-class history (Burrill 2019); settler workers as participants in 'accumulation by dispossession' who 'fight simultaneously over the distribution of wealth generated through their labour and the distribution of the colonial loot' (Englert 2020)","map_label":"Settler workers, settler order, 2019–20","evidence_note":"Burrill 2019 (abstract, existing record screq_burrill_2019; the strand cdn_working_class/indigenous_labour_settler_order carries him). Englert 2020 (read in full), conclusion: settler labour movements \"fight simultaneously over the distribution of wealth generated through their labour and the distribution of the colonial loot accumulated through the dispossession of the indigenous population\"; his cases are Palestine and South Africa, so the Canadian application is Burrill's. Re-proposes row 7 of the 2026-10-12 request, which is not on disk. (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-settler-colonial.md)","source_ids":["screq_burrill_2019","p4b_englert_2020"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review","target_strand":"cdn_working_class/indigenous_labour_settler_order"},{"proposal_id":"p4B_rel_16","source":"settler_colonialism","target":"environment","type":"connection","relationship_kind":"comparison","directed":false,"relationship":"Land as 'settler colonialism's specific, irreducible element': agriculture 'is inherently sedentary and, therefore, permanent' and 'progressively eats into Indigenous territory, a primitive accumulation that turns native flora and fauna into a dwindling resource' (Wolfe 2006); 'land is the irreducible element of settler colonialism' (Snelgrove et al. 2014)","map_label":"Land, agriculture, elimination","evidence_note":"Wolfe 2006 (read in full), fourth section: \"Of itself, however, modernity cannot explain the insatiable dynamic whereby settler colonialism always needs more land. The answer that springs most readily to mind is agriculture\"; \"Agriculture not only supports the other sectors. It is inherently sedentary and, therefore, permanent\"; \"The reproach of nomadism renders the native removable.\" Snelgrove, Dhamoon and Corntassel 2014, p. 30 (read): \"land is the irreducible element of settler colonialism, and … environmental degradation has often proceeded through and in support of settler colonialism\". Tuck and Yang 2012, p. 5 (read): \"Within settler colonialism, the most important concern is land/water/air/subterranean earth\". The dissertation evidence for the pairing is in the entry's scope_note, not here. Drawn by Agent B by the coordinator's decision; Agent C does not duplicate it. (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-settler-colonial.md)","source_ids":["screq_wolfe_2006","screq_snelgrove_dhamoon_corntassel_2014","screq_tuck_yang_2012"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review"}]
