inclusion does not establish Indigenous identity, citizenship, nation membership or external identity resolution; no Wikidata match recorded by this batch."},{"id":"mishuana_goeman","label":"Mishuana Goeman","identity_note":"University of California, Los Angeles, on the 2016 AICRJ memorial of Patrick Wolfe (read). Added in the period-4 wave of 2026-10-23. Roster inclusion does not establish Indigenous identity, citizenship, nation membership or external identity resolution; no Wikidata match recorded by this batch."},{"id":"renisa_mawani","label":"Renisa Mawani","identity_note":"Associate professor of sociology, University of British Columbia (publisher page, 2009); author of Colonial Proximities. Added in the period-4 wave of 2026-10-23. Roster inclusion does not establish Indigenous identity, citizenship, nation membership or external identity resolution; no Wikidata match recorded by this batch."},{"id":"jordan_stanger_ross","label":"Jordan Stanger-Ross","identity_note":"Editor of Landscapes of Injustice (McGill-Queen's, 2020); University of Victoria historian (the publisher page gives no biography). Added in the period-4 wave of 2026-10-23. Roster inclusion does not establish Indigenous identity, citizenship, nation membership or external identity resolution; no Wikidata match recorded by this batch."},{"id":"david_hugill","label":"David Hugill","identity_note":"Author of \"What Is a Settler-Colonial City?\" (Geography Compass, 2017; abstract read). Added in the period-4 wave of 2026-10-23. Roster inclusion does not establish Indigenous identity, citizenship, nation membership or external identity resolution; no Wikidata match recorded by this batch."}]
roster_additions [{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"sai_englert","role":"critic","context":"Marxist critique of 'the Wolfe-an model': elimination 'does not accurately define the overall logic of settler colonialism'; accumulation by dispossession 'carried out by all classes of settlers' (2020, read in full). Leiden.","works":"“Settlers, Workers, and the Logic of Accumulation by Dispossession” (2020); Settler Colonialism: An Introduction (2022, unread)","source_ids":["p4b_englert_2020"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"aileen_moreton_robinson","role":"contributor","context":"The nation as 'a white possession' built on 'the disavowal of Indigenous sovereignty'; 'patriarchal white sovereignty' (publisher page; as cited by Macoun and Strakosch and by Snelgrove et al.). QUT (publisher page); no identity assertion made here.","works":"The White Possessive (2015)","source_ids":["p4b_moreton_robinson_2015","p4b_macoun_strakosch_2013_qut","screq_snelgrove_dhamoon_corntassel_2014"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"corey_snelgrove","role":"critic","context":"Coauthor of a collective interview on the field's institutionalisation: it 'can displace, overshadow, or even mask over Indigenous studies'; Veracini's history erases Indigenous resistance; settler colonialism must be read as 'conditioned and contingent' (2014, read). UBC.","works":"“Unsettling Settler Colonialism” (2014), with Rita Kaur Dhamoon and Jeff Corntassel","source_ids":["screq_snelgrove_dhamoon_corntassel_2014"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"rita_kaur_dhamoon","role":"critic","context":"Coauthor; see Corey Snelgrove. UVic. Asks what anxieties 'are being masked over in the emergence and legitimacy of settler colonial studies, as a field distinct from Indigenous studies' (2014, p. 10).","works":"“Unsettling Settler Colonialism” (2014)","source_ids":["screq_snelgrove_dhamoon_corntassel_2014"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"jeff_corntassel","role":"critic","context":"Coauthor; see Corey Snelgrove. UVic. 'When settlers take up these questions, it's suddenly considered a legitimate field of study' (2014, p. 11); Indigenous resurgence as the organising frame.","works":"“Unsettling Settler Colonialism” (2014)","source_ids":["screq_snelgrove_dhamoon_corntassel_2014"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"mishuana_goeman","role":"contributor","context":"NAIS memorialist: Wolfe 'a key scholar in conceiving of a settler-colonial analytic in relation to Indigenous thinking'; his work 'a place to engage Indigenous studies concerns in relation to settler colonial studies' (2016, read). UCLA.","works":"“In Memoriam: Patrick Wolfe” (2016)","source_ids":["p4b_goeman_2016"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"james_rodger_miller","role":"historian","context":"Treaty-making in Canada (2009); unread; a distinctive riser among Canadian PhDs inside the Indigenous family (History PhD citation graph, release 2026-10-23); no use of the frame attested.","works":"Compact, Contract, Covenant (2009)","source_ids":["p4b_miller_2009"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"mary_jane_logan_mccallum","role":"historian","context":"Indigenous women's work 'in modern Native ways' and the state's placement programmes (2014, publisher page); beside the paradigm, not within it. University of Winnipeg.","works":"Indigenous Women, Work, and History, 1940–1980 (2014)","source_ids":["p4b_mccallum_2014"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"renisa_mawani","role":"historian","context":"Crossracial encounters and law in British Columbia's 'contact zone'; Indigenous dispossession and Chinese exclusion as one settler regime's racialisations (2009, publisher page). UBC sociology.","works":"Colonial Proximities (2009)","source_ids":["p4b_mawani_2009"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"jordan_stanger_ross","role":"historian","context":"Japanese Canadian internment reframed as dispossession, 'the deliberate and permanent destruction of home' (2020, publisher page); a reader quoted on the page calls Canada a 'settler colonial state'.","works":"ed., Landscapes of Injustice (2020)","source_ids":["p4b_stanger_ross_2020"],"basis":"source_review"}},{"node":"settler_colonialism","row":{"person_id":"david_hugill","role":"contributor","context":"Urbanises settler-colonial theory: the settler-colonial city in societies where colonists 'come to stay' and 'no formal process of decolonization has unfolded' (2017, abstract).","works":"“What Is a Settler-Colonial City?” (2017)","source_ids":["p4b_hugill_2017"],"basis":"source_review"}}]
people_identity_notes_for_existing_records {"lorenzo_veracini":"Historian, Institute for Social Research, Swinburne University of Technology (2011 biographical note, read); founding editor of Settler Colonial Studies. Wikidata Q112150999 (\"Australian historian\"; P106 political scientist, university teacher, historian; no birth date), checked by QLever SPARQL on 2026-10-23.","audra_simpson":"Anthropologist, Columbia University (Duke page; 2017 article). Wikidata Q112536616 (\"Kahnawà:ke Mohawk anthropologist\"; P569 1969; P108 Columbia, Cornell), checked by QLever SPARQL on 2026-10-23; the identity description is Wikidata's statement, not the project's.","glen_coulthard":"Political scientist, First Nations Studies Program and Department of Political Science, UBC (publisher page); the publisher and Englert identify him as Yellowknives Dene (their statement). Wikidata Q91710018 (\"Canadian scholar\"; P569 1974; P106 political scientist), checked by QLever SPARQL on 2026-10-23.","eve_tuck":"SUNY New Paltz on the 2012 article; University of Toronto per Wikidata Q28924966 (\"Indigenous studies scholar\"), checked by QLever SPARQL on 2026-10-23.","j_kehaulani_kauanui":"Professor of American Studies and Anthropology, Wesleyan University; co-founder of NAISA (author note on the 2016 essay, read). Wikidata Q59537273 (\"American Indigenous Studies professor\"; P569 1968-07-17; ORCID 0000-0002-2903-8155), newly found by QLever SPARQL on 2026-10-23 (the 2026-10-12 draft had none)."}

