proposed_edges [{"proposal_id":"p4C_rel_41","source":"environment","target":"indigenous","type":"connection","relationship_kind":"contribution","directed":true,"relationship":"Conservation as dispossession: Indian removal made the 'uninhabited wilderness' of Yellowstone, Glacier and Yosemite (Spence 1999); poachers and squatters against conservation (Warren 1997, Jacoby 2001); the Stoney excluded from Banff for game, sport and assimilation (Binnema and Niemi 2006); northern game laws as state authority over hunting cultures (Sandlos 2007)","map_label":"Conservation as dispossession, 1997–2007","evidence_note":"Spence's OUP abstract read; the Binnema–Niemi and Piper–Sandlos abstracts read; Sandlos's UBC Press description read; Jacoby and Warren known from Cronon's CV and Crossref only (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-environment.md §§6–7). Source strand environment/conservation_dispossession; target strand indigenous/land. Overlaps edge_696 (indigenous ↔ environment, a comparison through Huggins, Bullard, Cronon and Carruthers), which stays.","source_ids":["p4c_spence_dispossessing_1999","p4c_jacoby_crimes_2001","p4c_warren_hunters_1997","p4c_binnema_niemi_2006","p4c_sandlos_hunters_2007","p4c_cronon_cv"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review","target_strand":"indigenous/land"},{"proposal_id":"p4C_rel_42","source":"environment","target":"native_newcomer","type":"connection","relationship_kind":"contribution","directed":true,"relationship":"Canadian environmental histories of the fur-trade and northern worlds: the pemmican market that 'nearly wiped out the Canadian bison herds north of the Missouri River' (Colpitts 2014); ecological imperialism as 'a broken frontier' in the North (Piper and Sandlos 2007); Dene and Inuit hunters against conservationists (Sandlos 2007)","map_label":"Pemmican, the North and conservation, 2007–14","evidence_note":"Publisher descriptions and the 2007 abstract read; bodies unread (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-environment.md §6.3). Reduced strength. Source strand environment/canadian_environmental_history; target strand native_newcomer/fur_trade_national_economy.","source_ids":["p4c_colpitts_pemmican_2014","p4c_piper_sandlos_2007","p4c_sandlos_hunters_2007"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review","target_strand":"native_newcomer/fur_trade_national_economy"},{"proposal_id":"p4C_rel_43","source":"environment","target":"capitalismdebates","type":"connection","relationship_kind":"comparison","directed":false,"relationship":"Capital against the species: Malm's Fossil Capital (2016) holds that 'steam offered neither cheaper nor more abundant energy' but control over labour; Moore's Capitalism in the Web of Life (2015) and Stoll's 'A Metabolism of Society' (2014) ask what capitalism is for environmental historians; Worster had made agricultural capitalism 'the decisive factor' (1979)","map_label":"Capital, energy and the Anthropocene, 2014–16","evidence_note":"Malm's publisher page read; Moore metadata only; Stoll by chapter title in the Oxford Handbook contents; Worster's phrase as recorded in the graph's existing records (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-environment.md §9). A teaching comparison, not a reception claim. Source strand environment/anthropocene_climate.","source_ids":["p4c_malm_fossil_2016","p4c_moore_web_2015","p4c_isenberg_handbook_2014","worster_dust_bowl","pe131_cronon_place_stories_1992"],"classification_basis":"editorial_review"}]
