## 6. Canadian environmental history, 2001–2019

### 6.1 NiCHE (Network in Canadian History & Environment)

**Read status: read in full** (niche-canada.org/about/, 2026-10-23): "NiCHE was founded in fall 2004 by a small team of scholars"; in 2007 it "received a Social Sciences and Humanities Research Council of Canada Strategic Knowledge Clusters grant", stable funding to 2015; "a Canadian-based confederation of scholars of environmental history, environmental humanities, and historical geography" whose mandate is to "disseminate the research of those studying the historical relations between people and the rest of nature"; more than 400 members. Alan MacEachern (Western) "was director during the SSHRC Clusters years"; the Clusters-era executive included Graeme Wynn, William Turkel, Laura Cameron, Stéphane Castonguay, Colin Coates, Matthew Evenden and Liza Piper; Tina Loo sat on the advisory board. The graph already holds NiCHE's 2024 "Crash Course" page (`pe131_extras_niche_2024`).

