{"id":"p4a_manoff_2004","title":"Marlene Manoff, \"Theories of the Archive from Across the Disciplines,\" portal: Libraries and the Academy 4:1 (January 2004): 9–25.","citation":"Marlene Manoff, \"Theories of the Archive from Across the Disciplines,\" portal: Libraries and the Academy 4:1 (January 2004): 9–25.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1353/pla.2004.0015","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref and the MIT DSpace record (hdl.handle.net/1721.1/35687; abstract read: \"a confluence of interests among scholars, archivists, and librarians\"); the PDF bitstream returned an empty body and then HTTP 429; body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_mbembe_power_2002","title":"Achille Mbembe, \"The Power of the Archive and its Limits,\" in Carolyn Hamilton, Verne Harris, Jane Taylor, Michele Pickover, Graeme Reid and Razia Saleh, eds, Refiguring the Archive (Dordrecht: Kluwer, 2002), 19–27.","citation":"Achille Mbembe, \"The Power of the Archive and its Limits,\" in Carolyn Hamilton, Verne Harris, Jane Taylor, Michele Pickover, Graeme Reid and Razia Saleh, eds, Refiguring the Archive (Dordrecht: Kluwer, 2002), 19–27.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-010-0570-8_2","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Abstract opening read on Springer (\"The term 'archives' first refers to a building, a symbol of a public institution\"); the body is paywalled and unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_ottevaere_hnet_2004","title":"Dawn Ottevaere, review of Ann Stoler, Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power, H-Women, H-Net Reviews (June 2004).","citation":"Dawn Ottevaere, review of Ann Stoler, Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power, H-Women, H-Net Reviews (June 2004).","url":"https://www.h-net.org/reviews/showrev.php?id=9492","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Read in full for period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §6a); fetched with curl (H-Net permits redistribution with attribution). Quotes the book's pp. 9, 13, 15, 78, 83, 141, 162, 203 and gives \"Berkeley: University of California Press, 2002. xi + 335 pp.\""}}
{"id":"p4a_raben_bki_2009","title":"Remco Raben, \"Ambiguities of reading and writing\" [review of Stoler, Along the Archival Grain], Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde 165:4 (2009): 556–560.","citation":"Remco Raben, \"Ambiguities of reading and writing\" [review of Stoler, Along the Archival Grain], Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde 165:4 (2009): 556–560.","url":null,"verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"First page (p. 556) read at the foot of Gouda's PDF (UvA-DARE); the rest unread; the page range is inferred from the adjacent reviews. No URL of its own found."}}
{"id":"p4a_schulte_nordholt_bki_2009","title":"Henk Schulte Nordholt, \"How colonial is this effort to establish a new standard for an ethnography of the archive?\" [review of Stoler, Along the Archival Grain], Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde 165:4 (2009): 560–562.","citation":"Henk Schulte Nordholt, \"How colonial is this effort to establish a new standard for an ethnography of the archive?\" [review of Stoler, Along the Archival Grain], Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde 165:4 (2009): 560–562.","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/11245/1.311281","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Read in full (UvA-DARE final published version) for period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §2a); quotes the book's pp. 32–33, 35 and 45. The PDF also prints the first paragraph of Stoler's reply (p. 562)."}}
{"id":"p4a_schultz_hnet_2015","title":"Ronald Schultz, review of Ann Laura Stoler, ed., Imperial Debris: On Ruins and Ruination, H-Empire, H-Net Reviews (February 2015).","citation":"Ronald Schultz, review of Ann Laura Stoler, ed., Imperial Debris: On Ruins and Ruination, H-Empire, H-Net Reviews (February 2015).","url":"https://www.h-net.org/reviews/showrev.php?id=41934","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Read in full (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §6c); quotes pp. 7 and 9 of Stoler's \"The Rot Remains\" and gives the book's ISBNs and 384 pp."}}
{"id":"p4a_schwartz_cook_2002","title":"Joan M. Schwartz and Terry Cook, \"Archives, Records, and Power: The Making of Modern Memory,\" Archival Science 2:1–2 (March 2002): 1–19.","citation":"Joan M. Schwartz and Terry Cook, \"Archives, Records, and Power: The Making of Modern Memory,\" Archival Science 2:1–2 (March 2002): 1–19.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02435628","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Abstract, keywords and reference list read on Springer (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §3): \"Archives, then, are not passive storehouses of old stuff, but active sites where social power is negotiated\"; references cite Derrida and Verne Harris, not Foucault, Stoler or Trouillot. Body paywalled and unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_sepinwall_2013","title":"Alyssa Goldstein Sepinwall, \"Still Unthinkable? The Haitian Revolution and the Reception of Michel-Rolph Trouillot's Silencing the Past,\" Journal of Haitian Studies 19:2 (Fall 2013): 75–103.","citation":"Alyssa Goldstein Sepinwall, \"Still Unthinkable? The Haitian Revolution and the Reception of Michel-Rolph Trouillot's Silencing the Past,\" Journal of Haitian Studies 19:2 (Fall 2013): 75–103.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1353/jhs.2013.0036","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref (issued September 2013); Project MUSE challenge page; unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_steedman_dust_2002","title":"Carolyn Steedman, Dust: The Archive and Cultural History (Manchester: Manchester University Press, 2001; New Brunswick: Rutgers University Press, 2002).","citation":"Carolyn Steedman, Dust: The Archive and Cultural History (Manchester: Manchester University Press, 2001; New Brunswick: Rutgers University Press, 2002).","url":"https://www.rutgersuniversitypress.org/dust/9780813530475/","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Rutgers page read (1 February 2002, 208 pp., description: \"archivization\"; the archive as the repository of \"that which will not go away\"); Manchester page 403; body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_steedman_fever_2001","title":"Carolyn Steedman, \"Something She Called a Fever: Michelet, Derrida, and Dust,\" American Historical Review 106:4 (October 2001): 1159–1180.","citation":"Carolyn Steedman, \"Something She Called a Fever: Michelet, Derrida, and Dust,\" American Historical Review 106:4 (October 2001): 1159–1180.","url":"https://doi.org/10.2307/2692943","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref and the Warwick repository record (wrap.warwick.ac.uk/11562; no full text); unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_archival_grain_2009","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, Along the Archival Grain: Epistemic Anxieties and Colonial Common Sense (Princeton: Princeton University Press, 2009).","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, Along the Archival Grain: Epistemic Anxieties and Colonial Common Sense (Princeton: Princeton University Press, 2009).","url":"https://muse.jhu.edu/book/61029","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Project MUSE book record: summary and contents with page ranges read (Prologue in Two Parts 1–16; The Pulse of the Archive 17–54; chs 3–7; appendices; © 2008 on the record; Gouda gives \"2009. xiii + 314 pp.\"). Princeton's page and chapter PDF returned 403; the body is unread; every quotation is as given by Gouda or Schulte Nordholt with their page numbers (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §2)."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_archives_2002","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance,\" Archival Science 2:1–2 (March 2002): 87–109.","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance,\" Archival Science 2:1–2 (March 2002): 87–109.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02435632","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Springer page: abstract, keywords and reference list read for period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §1); the body is paywalled and unread. Crossref: vol. 2, issue 1–2, pp. 87–109, March 2002. The abstract carries \"from archive-as-source to archive-as-subject\"; the notes cite Foucault, Derrida, Trouillot, Richards, Dirks and Cohn."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_bki_reply_2009","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Thinking through colonial ontologies,\" Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde 165:4 (2009): 562–.","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Thinking through colonial ontologies,\" Bijdragen tot de Taal-, Land- en Volkenkunde 165:4 (2009): 562–.","url":null,"verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"First paragraph read at the foot of Schulte Nordholt's PDF; the end page is unknown and the reply unread; Brill's issue page returned 403. No URL of its own found."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_carnal_2002","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power: Race and the Intimate in Colonial Rule (Berkeley: University of California Press, 2002; 2nd ed. with a new preface, 2010).","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power: Race and the Intimate in Colonial Rule (Berkeley: University of California Press, 2002; 2nd ed. with a new preface, 2010).","url":"https://www.ucpress.edu/books/carnal-knowledge-and-imperial-power/paper","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"UC Press page for the 2010 edition read: description, contents (chs 1–7 and epilogue), author line. The 2002 edition's pagination is taken from Ottevaere's review (p4a_ottevaere_hnet_2004). Body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_debris_2013","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, ed., Imperial Debris: On Ruins and Ruination (Durham: Duke University Press, 2013).","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, ed., Imperial Debris: On Ruins and Ruination (Durham: Duke University Press, 2013).","url":"https://www.dukeupress.edu/imperial-debris","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Duke page not fetched this session; the details (2013, 384 pp., ISBN 978-0-8223-5361-4 paper) are from Schultz's review. Body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_duress_2016","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, Duress: Imperial Durabilities in Our Times (Durham: Duke University Press, 2016).","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, Duress: Imperial Durabilities in Our Times (Durham: Duke University Press, 2016).","url":"https://www.dukeupress.edu/duress","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Description, contents and review excerpts read (November 2016, 448 pp.); body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_haunted_2006","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, ed., Haunted by Empire: Geographies of Intimacy in North American History (Durham: Duke University Press, 2006).","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, ed., Haunted by Empire: Geographies of Intimacy in North American History (Durham: Duke University Press, 2006).","url":"https://www.dukeupress.edu/haunted-by-empire","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Description and contents read (May 2006, 568 pp.; Stoler's \"Intimidations of Empire\" p. 1 and \"Tense and Tender Ties\" p. 23; Hall's commentary, Cott's afterword). Bodies unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_newschool_profile","title":"The New School for Social Research, faculty page \"Ann Stoler.\"","citation":"The New School for Social Research, faculty page \"Ann Stoler.\"","url":"https://www.newschool.edu/nssr/faculty/ann-stoler/","verification":{"status":"not_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"The page returned HTTP 429 on three attempts on 2026-10-23; its content is known only through a search engine's rendering (Willy Brandt Distinguished University Professor of Anthropology and Historical Studies; University of Michigan 1989–2003; at the New School since 2004 as founding chair of the revitalised Anthropology Department; director of the Institute for Critical Social Inquiry). Re-fetch before relying on it."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_refiguring_2002","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance: On the Content in the Form,\" in Carolyn Hamilton et al., eds, Refiguring the Archive (Dordrecht: Kluwer, 2002), 83–102.","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance: On the Content in the Form,\" in Carolyn Hamilton et al., eds, Refiguring the Archive (Dordrecht: Kluwer, 2002), 83–102.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-010-0570-8_7","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref only; the reprint of the Archival Science essay. Unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_stoler_tense_2001","title":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Tense and Tender Ties: The Politics of Comparison in North American History and (Post) Colonial Studies,\" Journal of American History 88:3 (December 2001): 829–865.","citation":"Ann Laura Stoler, \"Tense and Tender Ties: The Politics of Comparison in North American History and (Post) Colonial Studies,\" Journal of American History 88:3 (December 2001): 829–865.","url":"https://doi.org/10.2307/2700385","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref (first page 829, December 2001); the last page is not confirmed; unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_taylor_archive_repertoire_2003","title":"Diana Taylor, The Archive and the Repertoire: Performing Cultural Memory in the Americas (Durham: Duke University Press, 2003).","citation":"Diana Taylor, The Archive and the Repertoire: Performing Cultural Memory in the Americas (Durham: Duke University Press, 2003).","url":"https://www.dukeupress.edu/the-archive-and-the-repertoire","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Description, date (September 2003, 352 pp.) and prizes read; body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_trouillot_global_2003","title":"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, Global Transformations: Anthropology and the Modern World (New York: Palgrave Macmillan, 2003).","citation":"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, Global Transformations: Anthropology and the Modern World (New York: Palgrave Macmillan, 2003).","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-137-04144-9","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Springer book page read: description, contents with page ranges (Introduction 1–5; Anthropology and the Savage Slot 7–28; North Atlantic Fictions 29–46; A Fragmented Globality 47–78; The Anthropology of the State 79–96; Adieu, Culture 97–116; Making Sense 117–139), author line, print date 27 January 2004 (© 2003). Body unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_trouillot_papers_ead","title":"University of Chicago Library, Hanna Holborn Gray Special Collections Research Center, \"Guide to the Michel-Rolph Trouillot Papers\" (finding aid).","citation":"University of Chicago Library, Hanna Holborn Gray Special Collections Research Center, \"Guide to the Michel-Rolph Trouillot Papers\" (finding aid).","url":"https://www.lib.uchicago.edu/ead/rlg/ICU.SPCL.TROUILLOTMR.pdf","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Biographical note read in full from the PDF text layer (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §4e): left Haiti 1968; Brooklyn College BA 1978; PhD Johns Hopkins 1985 under Mintz and Price; Duke 1983–88; Johns Hopkins from 1988, Krieger/Eisenhower Professor, founder-director of the Institute for Global Studies in Culture, History, and Power; Chicago 1998–2012. Inventory folder titles consulted for dates (chair 1993–96)."}}
{"id":"p4a_trouillot_remixed_2021","title":"Yarimar Bonilla, Greg Beckett and Mayanthi L. Fernando, eds, Trouillot Remixed: The Michel-Rolph Trouillot Reader (Durham: Duke University Press, 2021).","citation":"Yarimar Bonilla, Greg Beckett and Mayanthi L. Fernando, eds, Trouillot Remixed: The Michel-Rolph Trouillot Reader (Durham: Duke University Press, 2021).","url":"https://www.dukeupress.edu/trouillot-remixed","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Description, contents, author line (\"Michel-Rolph Trouillot (1949–2012) was Professor of Anthropology and Social Sciences at the University of Chicago\") and blurbs read (December 2021, 456 pp.). The volume contains no essay by David Scott. Bodies unread."}}
{"id":"p4a_trouillot_savage_slot_2003","title":"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, \"Anthropology and the Savage Slot: The Poetics and Politics of Otherness,\" in Global Transformations (New York: Palgrave Macmillan, 2003), 7–28; first in Richard G. Fox, ed., Recapturing Anthropology (Santa Fe: School of American Research Press, 1991).","citation":"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, \"Anthropology and the Savage Slot: The Poetics and Politics of Otherness,\" in Global Transformations (New York: Palgrave Macmillan, 2003), 7–28; first in Richard G. Fox, ed., Recapturing Anthropology (Santa Fe: School of American Research Press, 1991).","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-137-04144-9_2","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Chapter abstract read on Springer (\"Anthropology discovered globalization before the term became fashionable\"); the preview is not displayed; the 1991 first printing is not stated on the page and is not verified (Trouillot Remixed lists the essay first; the obituary names it among his works)."}}
{"id":"p4a_trouillot_silencing_1995","title":"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, Silencing the Past: Power and the Production of History (Boston: Beacon Press, 1995; 20th-anniversary edition with a foreword by Hazel V. Carby, 2015).","citation":"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, Silencing the Past: Power and the Production of History (Boston: Beacon Press, 1995; 20th-anniversary edition with a foreword by Hazel V. Carby, 2015).","url":"https://www.beacon.org/Silencing-the-Past-P1109.aspx","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Beacon page for the 2015 edition read: description, contents (Preface; 1 The Power in the Story; 2 The Three Faces of Sans Souci; 3 An Unthinkable History; 4 Good Day, Columbus; 5 The Presence in the Past; Epilogue), date 17 March 2015, ISBN 9780807080535. The 1995 date (21 November 1995) rests on a trade listing seen in a search rendering. The body is unread: the four-moments passage of ch. 1 is given as later writers list it and as Davidson (p4a_davidson_overland_2020) quotes it without pages; p. 98 as quoted by Craipain (p4a_craipain_hnet_2024). Wording awaits re-verification on a library copy."}}
{"id":"p4a_trouillot_uchicago_obit_2012","title":"William Harms, \"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, scholar of Caribbean history, 1949–2012,\" University of Chicago News, 10 July 2012.","citation":"William Harms, \"Michel-Rolph Trouillot, scholar of Caribbean history, 1949–2012,\" University of Chicago News, 10 July 2012.","url":"https://news.uchicago.edu/story/michel-rolph-trouillot-scholar-caribbean-history-1949-2012","verification":{"status":"supporting_page_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Read in full for period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md §4a): death 5 July 2012 aged 62; BA CUNY 1978; PhD Johns Hopkins 1985; Johns Hopkins chair and institute; Chicago 1998; works 1977–2003; 2011 Fanon award; colleagues quoted."}}
{"id":"p4a_zeitlyn_2012","title":"David Zeitlyn, \"Anthropology in and of the Archives: Possible Futures and Contingent Pasts. Archives as Anthropological Surrogates,\" Annual Review of Anthropology 41 (2012): 461–480.","citation":"David Zeitlyn, \"Anthropology in and of the Archives: Possible Futures and Contingent Pasts. Archives as Anthropological Surrogates,\" Annual Review of Anthropology 41 (2012): 461–480.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-anthro-092611-145721","verification":{"status":"bibliographic_metadata_checked","checked_on":"2026-10-23","note":"Crossref (21 October 2012); the Annual Reviews page returned 403; unread."}}

exec
/bin/bash -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
import json,unicodedata,re,difflib
p=json.load(open('data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/release/editorial-additions.json'));g=json.load(open('historiography-1920-2000.json'))
print('people type',type(g['people']).__name__)
old=list(g['people'].values()) if isinstance(g['people'],dict) else g['people']
norm=lambda s: re.sub('["'^a-z]'"','',unicodedata.normalize('NFKD',s.lower()))
for n in p['new_people']:
 matches=[]
 for o in old:
  a,b=norm(n['label']),norm(o['label'])
  if a==b or (len(a)>8 and difflib.SequenceMatcher(None,a,b).ratio()>.82):matches.append((o['id'],o['label']))
 print(n['id'],n['label'], 'MATCHES',matches,'NOTE',n.get('identity_note'))
print('UPDATES',json.dumps(p['people_updates'],ensure_ascii=False))
