{"node":"post","field":"context","person_id":"ann_laura_stoler","new":"Reworks Foucault through colonial archives, race and sexuality (1995); treats 'colonizer/colonized' as 'a historically shifting pair of social categories that needs to be explained' (2002, p. 13, as quoted by Ottevaere); asks scholars to move 'from archive-as-source to archive-as-subject' (2002). Gouda: homage to her work 'has become de rigueur' in postcolonial studies (2009).","reason":"Period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md P.6): the row rested on one publisher description; Ottevaere 2004 and Gouda 2009 read in full, the 2002 abstract read."}
