{"node":"queer","field":"context","person_id":"ann_laura_stoler","new":"Colonial archives and racial formation expose limits and possibilities in Foucauldian histories of sexuality (1995); 'sexual control was both an instrumental image for the body politic … and itself fundamental to how racial policies were secured' (2002, p. 78, as quoted by Ottevaere).","reason":"Period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md P.6): Ottevaere 2004 read in full."}
