{"node":"gender","field":"context","person_id":"ann_laura_stoler","new":"Makes colonial race and sexuality central to a critical extension of Foucault (1995); 'Ethnographies of empire should attend both to changing sensibilities and to sex' (2002, p. 78, as quoted by Ottevaere), who compares her evaluation of 'historically designated categories' to Joan Scott's.","reason":"Period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md P.6): Ottevaere 2004 read in full."}
