{"node":"post","field":"focus","strand":"colonial_intimacies","new":"Empire becomes part of the history of European bourgeois sexuality (1995). Carnal Knowledge and Imperial Power (2002) made 'the intimate' a matter of state and 'colonizer/colonized' a shifting pair of categories (p. 13, as quoted by Ottevaere); the same year her 'Colonial Archives and the Arts of Governance' moved 'from archive-as-source to archive-as-subject', the programme now carried by the entry archival_turn.","reason":"Period-4 wave 1 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-archive.md P.9 3): the strand rested on one publisher description; cross-reference to the new entry."}
