{"node":"settler_colonialism","field":"context","new":"Defends Wolfe's theory against its reduction to a slogan and against the charge of an Anglo binary, while insisting that 'Settler Colonial Studies does not, should not, and cannot replace Indigenous Studies' and that indigeneity is a category of analysis distinct from race (2016, read in full). Co-founder of NAISA (2008). Wesleyan; Wikidata Q59537273.","reason":"Period-4 wave 1, 2026-10-23 (data/extension-2026/period4-wave1-2026-10-23/evidence-settler-colonial.md) P.3: roster row amended from the texts read.","person_id":"j_kehaulani_kauanui"}
