p4b_mccallum_2014 https://uofmpress.ca/books/detail/indigenous-women-work-and-history bibliographic_metadata_checked Publisher page read (May 2014; contents, including the conclusion "The Wages of Whiteness and the Indigenous Historian"; Manitoba Day Award 2016; author Professor of History, University of Winnipeg). The description (fetch summary) speaks of women who worked "in 'modern Native ways'" and of state placement programmes serving "assimilation and the extinguishment of treaty obligations"; it does not use "settler colonialism". Unread.
p4b_miller_2009 None not_checked Publisher page not found; ISBNs 9780802097415 (hardback) and 9780802095152 (paperback) from library and retailer records. Unread. A distinctive riser among Canadian PhDs inside the Indigenous family (History PhD citation graph, release 2026-10-23); no use of the settler-colonial frame is attested.
